JET_CLI_EFFECT_SOURCE :: "// D-META-ONE1=A: the effect vocabulary is written here, not in Rust.\n//\n// This is ordinary Jet source. Each line declares one effect root or leaf.\n// Effect parsing, marker arguments (`#FX(Net, FS)`), fact registration,\n// manifest and `--allow`/`--deny` validation, diagnostics, and reflection all\n// read this list (Foundation's generated Registry/EffectVocabulary.jet carries\n// it to the compiler), so an effect exists exactly when it is written here.\n// A root with leaves is closed: a dotted name under it must be one of them.\n// The roots' order is the canonical order of a written effect row.\n// `Panic`, `Mem` and `Time.Wait` are deny-only: a policy may refuse them but\n// never has to grant them.\n\neffect Net $irreversible\neffect FS\neffect FS.Read\neffect FS.Write $irreversible\neffect IO\neffect DB\neffect DB.Read\neffect DB.Write\neffect Time\neffect Time.Wait\neffect Rand\neffect Rand.Draw\neffect Env\neffect Exec $irreversible\neffect Exec.Exit\neffect Exec.Args\neffect Log\neffect GPU\neffect FFI $irreversible\neffect FFI.Go\neffect FFI.Java\neffect FFI.DotNet\neffect FFI.Fortran\neffect FFI.Cobol\neffect FFI.Tcl\neffect FFI.Lua\neffect FFI.Ada\neffect FFI.Pascal\neffect FFI.Dart\neffect FFI.PowerShell\neffect FFI.Perl\neffect FFI.Ruby\neffect FFI.Php\neffect FFI.R\neffect FFI.Com\neffect FFI.C\neffect FFI.Cpp\neffect FFI.Asm\neffect FFI.Py\neffect FFI.Octave\neffect Browser\neffect Secret\neffect Panic\neffect Mem\neffect Mem.Alloc\neffect Mem.Rc\n"

